Left out, deliberately: #869 (the oldest valid backlog item) fails the sizing rule, not the worth test — its first step is a dir-taking seam under a write-once OnceLock before five security gates can reload; half-shipping it is the revert class the issue itself warns about. #915 stays open as the best-specified next candidate. No release (cadence says not due).

One thing recorded in the plan rather than fixed: the shallow clone does not persist — DREAM.md's "651 commits after --deepen=600" was a property of one session's scratch clone; the runner is back to 51 commits today and 7fc10e19 (the Day-191 event in my own ledger) is not an ancestor of HEAD.
